WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:04.779
It was a beautiful September day, but Shaun
Taylor was trapped in his car in one of the

00:00:04.779 --> 00:00:07.839
worst cases of gridlock he had ever seen.

00:00:07.839 --> 00:00:12.030
He tried to look on the bright side though,
and while he was stuck in an unmoving car,

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:17.039
at least he had a pleasant view of the wide,
shimmering lake just off the road next to

00:00:17.039 --> 00:00:18.039
him.

00:00:18.039 --> 00:00:22.010
He was admiring the scene when tiny drops
of rain started landing on his windshield.

00:00:22.010 --> 00:00:25.619
That’s funny, there wasn’t a cloud in
the sky a moment ago.

00:00:25.619 --> 00:00:27.710
There was something off about the rain though.

00:00:27.710 --> 00:00:30.770
It looked dirty, a rusty red color.

00:00:30.770 --> 00:00:31.770
Was that… blood?

00:00:31.770 --> 00:00:37.870
He didn’t have time to think about it, because
just then a thick, dense mist began to roll

00:00:37.870 --> 00:00:38.980
over the lake.

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:41.650
A fog of blood.

00:00:41.650 --> 00:00:46.040
Just off the side of the road, he could see
a huge silhouette rising out of the water.

00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:47.910
Is that an old submarine?

00:00:47.910 --> 00:00:54.010
What Shaun didn’t know was that he was about
to have an encounter with SCP - 1861, also

00:00:54.010 --> 00:01:01.230
known as The HMS Wintersheimer - a ghostly
submarine with strange and terrifying effects.

00:01:01.230 --> 00:01:05.829
Shaun and the other drivers stuck in traffic
that day were far from the first people to

00:01:05.829 --> 00:01:11.119
have a dangerous brush with this legendary
vessel - according to SCP Foundation records,

00:01:11.119 --> 00:01:16.710
the HMS Wintersheimer has been appearing since
as early as 1916.

00:01:16.710 --> 00:01:21.560
The first recorded incident occurred in the
British seaside town of Innsmouth-On-Sea.

00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:26.250
You won’t find this town on any maps, or
in the history books, and you’re about to

00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:27.700
find out why.

00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:32.189
The 500-person population of the town, which
had already reduced by the wartime draft into

00:01:32.189 --> 00:01:38.909
the currently-raging Great World War, awoke
to red skies on February 6th, 1916.

00:01:38.909 --> 00:01:44.499
Citizens left their homes to investigate,
only to find their entire town had been enveloped

00:01:44.499 --> 00:01:46.299
in a thick, red mist.

00:01:46.299 --> 00:01:52.650
The swelling, crimson clouds up ahead began
to rain, showering the town in a hail of viscous,

00:01:52.650 --> 00:01:53.880
red goop.

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:58.170
Anyone unlucky enough to taste it would say
that this strange rain was a dreadful mix

00:01:58.170 --> 00:02:00.079
of salt and copper.

00:02:00.079 --> 00:02:05.680
This was because, as the Foundation would
later determine, the rain and fog was a disgusting

00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:11.380
combination of saltwater, human blood, and
human cerebrospinal fluid.

00:02:11.380 --> 00:02:15.380
But the real threat was rising, just beyond
the beach.

00:02:15.380 --> 00:02:22.330
Technically speaking, the HMS Wintersheimer
vessel is designated as SCP - 1861 - A. It

00:02:22.330 --> 00:02:27.270
appears to be a World War One-era British
B-Class Submarine, designed by Vickers for

00:02:27.270 --> 00:02:29.640
the Royal Navy in 1904.

00:02:29.640 --> 00:02:35.210
By 1916, this particular type of boat was
already on its way to being obsolete, and

00:02:35.210 --> 00:02:39.330
were largely deployed in Malta, far from the
active fronts.

00:02:39.330 --> 00:02:44.070
So one of these vessels appearing on an otherwise
unremarkable stretch of English coastline

00:02:44.070 --> 00:02:48.740
should have been a clue that something was
terribly wrong - but the poor residents of

00:02:48.740 --> 00:02:52.030
Innsmouth-On-Sea didn’t know the half of
it.

00:02:52.030 --> 00:02:57.320
Soon, figures in what appeared to be archaic
diving gear began emerging from the Wintersheimer,

00:02:57.320 --> 00:02:59.100
and made their way into the township.

00:02:59.100 --> 00:03:04.220
They seemed terrified, running up to and frantically
screaming at any local they could find.

00:03:04.220 --> 00:03:07.510
“Please listen to me, something terrible
is about to happen here.

00:03:07.510 --> 00:03:09.980
We need you to come with us or you’re all
going to die.

00:03:09.980 --> 00:03:11.540
You must believe us!”

00:03:11.540 --> 00:03:13.620
The locals were frightened by what they heard.

00:03:13.620 --> 00:03:17.870
They’d been listening to news reports of
the Great War unfolding across the globe for

00:03:17.870 --> 00:03:19.320
two years now.

00:03:19.320 --> 00:03:20.910
Had it finally come to them?

00:03:20.910 --> 00:03:25.180
They pictured shells raining down from the
sky, decimating their defenseless little town

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:26.870
in a rain of fire.

00:03:26.870 --> 00:03:31.040
The Navy must have been brought in to save
them before the German bombardment began.

00:03:31.040 --> 00:03:37.910
While some took more convincing than others,
the men in diving suits - known as SCP - 1861

00:03:37.910 --> 00:03:43.400
- B - eventually managed to persuade the entire
town to join them, and lead the townspeople

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:44.970
down to the water.

00:03:44.970 --> 00:03:48.480
One by one, they were all boarded onto the
submarine.

00:03:48.480 --> 00:03:49.480
Hundreds of them.

00:03:49.480 --> 00:03:52.950
Many couldn’t believe their eyes as they
watched scores of people disappear in front

00:03:52.950 --> 00:03:56.080
of them into the dark bowels of the Wintersheimer.

00:03:56.080 --> 00:03:57.430
Where were they all going?

00:03:57.430 --> 00:03:58.810
How would they all fit in there?

00:03:58.810 --> 00:04:02.340
But it was too late for any of them to back
out now.

00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:06.790
The vessel submerged once more, and everyone
was gone.

00:04:06.790 --> 00:04:12.180
The entire population of Innsmouth-On-Sea
had disappeared in a rain and fog of blood,

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:14.100
never to be seen again.

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:18.729
The Foundation wiped all records of the town
from existence and delivered appropriate amnestic

00:04:18.729 --> 00:04:23.460
treatment to anyone who still mentioned or
remembered Innsmouth-On-Sea.

00:04:23.460 --> 00:04:29.219
The fate of those who board the HMS Wintersheimer
is always the same - vanished from the face

00:04:29.219 --> 00:04:34.389
of the earth, explained away by the Foundation
as “accidental death by extreme weather

00:04:34.389 --> 00:04:35.389
event.”

00:04:35.389 --> 00:04:40.700
There have been hundreds of documented sightings
of SCP - 1861, and the anomalous weather event

00:04:40.700 --> 00:04:46.870
can occur near any body of water wide enough
to accommodate SCP-1861-A’s comms tower

00:04:46.870 --> 00:04:48.729
and topmost platform.

00:04:48.729 --> 00:04:53.530
Depth does not seem to be any hindrance to
the submarine appearing and it can even manifest

00:04:53.530 --> 00:04:56.960
in water that’s just a few inches deep.

00:04:56.960 --> 00:05:00.909
As Shaun and the other unfortunate victims
of the rush hour traffic were being showered

00:05:00.909 --> 00:05:06.490
in thick, red droplets from above, a crimson
mist rolled in between the cars.

00:05:06.490 --> 00:05:10.749
Shaun had heard of so-called freak weather
events before - like raining frogs and fish

00:05:10.749 --> 00:05:14.340
- but this was something different, and it
frightened him.

00:05:14.340 --> 00:05:18.639
He could see now that the silhouette rising
from the lake really was an old submarine,

00:05:18.639 --> 00:05:23.360
and he watched as a legion of mysterious figures
disembarked from the vessel and began spilling

00:05:23.360 --> 00:05:24.529
onto the road.

00:05:24.529 --> 00:05:28.699
The men in ancient-looking diving suits walked
among the cars and one of them approached

00:05:28.699 --> 00:05:29.789
Shaun’s car.

00:05:29.789 --> 00:05:34.169
He began tapping frantically on the window
and Shaun could tell he was yelling something.

00:05:34.169 --> 00:05:39.539
Shaun was scared and more, but more than anything
else, he was confused.

00:05:39.539 --> 00:05:43.430
Against his better judgement, he rolled down
the window, just a crack, to hear what the

00:05:43.430 --> 00:05:44.620
man was saying.

00:05:44.620 --> 00:05:49.610
His British accented voice muted by the diving
suit, the man frantically told him “Sir!

00:05:49.610 --> 00:05:50.610
Please listen to me!

00:05:50.610 --> 00:05:53.340
I’m Lieutenant Samuel Ramsey of the HMS
Wintersheimer.

00:05:53.340 --> 00:05:54.960
We're evacuating the area.

00:05:54.960 --> 00:05:56.730
Please, you've got to come with me.

00:05:56.730 --> 00:05:58.660
You're in danger out here.”

00:05:58.660 --> 00:05:59.660
“HMS?”

00:05:59.660 --> 00:06:01.860
Shaun thought, “isn’t that what they call
British ships?

00:06:01.860 --> 00:06:05.729
What was a British submarine doing in the
middle of a lake in the United States?”

00:06:05.729 --> 00:06:10.189
Through his windshield, Shaun could already
see other men in diving suits leading people

00:06:10.189 --> 00:06:13.259
from the cars out towards the submarine.

00:06:13.259 --> 00:06:15.449
Something had to be going on here.

00:06:15.449 --> 00:06:16.449
Something big.

00:06:16.449 --> 00:06:21.020
Lieutenant Ramsey was still banging away at
the glass of Shaun’s window, becoming increasingly

00:06:21.020 --> 00:06:22.020
agitated.

00:06:22.020 --> 00:06:25.159
“Sir, if you won’t comply with my orders,
I’m within my rights to take you by force

00:06:25.159 --> 00:06:26.629
- for your own safety.”

00:06:26.629 --> 00:06:30.690
Shaun could feel the fear setting in but he
didn’t know what else to do.

00:06:30.690 --> 00:06:33.110
He turned off the car and took off his seatbelt.

00:06:33.110 --> 00:06:37.650
He was just about to open the door when there
was a tap on the passenger side window of

00:06:37.650 --> 00:06:38.650
his car.

00:06:38.650 --> 00:06:41.910
It was a soldier in what looked to be advanced
tactical gear.

00:06:41.910 --> 00:06:45.749
There were several soldiers directing cars
to drive on the shoulder to get around the

00:06:45.749 --> 00:06:47.620
mess of stopped automobiles.

00:06:47.620 --> 00:06:51.580
Shaun looked to his left and the man in the
diving suit was gone.

00:06:51.580 --> 00:06:55.550
The soldier tapped again and Shaun didn’t
need to be told twice.

00:06:55.550 --> 00:06:59.919
He followed his directions and drove around
the traffic jam and out of the mist.

00:06:59.919 --> 00:07:04.199
A half mile down the road, Shaun was stopped
by another group of soldiers and given an

00:07:04.199 --> 00:07:05.199
amnestic.

00:07:05.199 --> 00:07:12.909
He drove away never knowing how close he had
come to vanishing in the bowels of SCP-1861-A.

00:07:12.909 --> 00:07:18.620
Shaun was lucky that one of the SCP Foundation’s
Mobile Task Forces had taken over the situation,

00:07:18.620 --> 00:07:24.479
but they were too late to help those who had
already complied with SCP - 1861 - B’s orders

00:07:24.479 --> 00:07:26.339
and boarded the Wintersheimer.

00:07:26.339 --> 00:07:30.340
The Task Force made it their business to save
whoever they could, but that wasn’t their

00:07:30.340 --> 00:07:36.870
only directive: The Foundation had recorded
a huge number of SCP - 1861 instances since

00:07:36.870 --> 00:07:43.220
1916, and now, they were finally going to
figure out what was going on inside.

00:07:43.220 --> 00:07:46.839
The Foundation had already discovered that
those taken onto the Wintersheimer don’t

00:07:46.839 --> 00:07:51.520
simply disappear - once on board the submarine
they are forced into a diving suit of their

00:07:51.520 --> 00:07:59.779
own, which transforms them into new instances
of SCP - 1861 - B. Upon realizing this, Foundation

00:07:59.779 --> 00:08:02.620
scientists devised an ingenious plot.

00:08:02.620 --> 00:08:07.740
Six months before this latest instance of
1861, the Foundation dispatched two members

00:08:07.740 --> 00:08:12.440
of D-Class personnel who were familiar with
one another into the red mist.

00:08:12.440 --> 00:08:19.069
One was instructed not to interact with SCP
- 1861 - B, while the other, named Sal, was

00:08:19.069 --> 00:08:21.210
ordered to enter the submarine.

00:08:21.210 --> 00:08:25.619
His mission was to report back all findings
to Foundation researcher Dr. Klutch during

00:08:25.619 --> 00:08:27.969
the next 1861 event.

00:08:27.969 --> 00:08:31.990
The D-Class who remained on shore was brought
in once more by the Mobile Task Force during

00:08:31.990 --> 00:08:34.409
the September event that Shaun witnessed.

00:08:34.409 --> 00:08:38.969
They checked each diving suit-wearing anomaly
until they heard a familiar voice, muffled

00:08:38.969 --> 00:08:47.090
by the mask: It was Sal, and he’d been transformed
into an instance of SCP - 1861 - B. The human

00:08:47.090 --> 00:08:52.350
D-Class, receiving questions from Dr. Klutch
via a remote broadcast, commenced the interview

00:08:52.350 --> 00:08:53.860
of his former friend.

00:08:53.860 --> 00:08:58.160
It is from this vital interview that much
of the Foundation’s knowledge of the mysterious

00:08:58.160 --> 00:09:00.610
HMS Wintersheimer is drawn.

00:09:00.610 --> 00:09:05.620
According to Sal, the interior of the Wintersheimer
- which is a long, narrow, passageway - is

00:09:05.620 --> 00:09:09.230
a spatial anomaly that seems to stretch on
forever.

00:09:09.230 --> 00:09:13.740
This explains how vast numbers of people,
like the entire population of Innsmouth-On-Sea,

00:09:13.740 --> 00:09:17.019
can disappear into the submarine at once.

00:09:17.019 --> 00:09:22.029
Sal reported that, about an hour after entering
the vessel, the hatch closed and the interior

00:09:22.029 --> 00:09:27.970
began rapidly filling with water as the submarine
descended.Prisoners of the Wintersheimer were

00:09:27.970 --> 00:09:32.019
faced with two choices: Suit up… or drown.

00:09:32.019 --> 00:09:38.100
Few chose the latter option, and as soon as
the suit was on, the transformation had begun.

00:09:38.100 --> 00:09:43.019
As soon as everyone was suited up and the
submarine had fully descended, causing the

00:09:43.019 --> 00:09:47.170
1861 weather event to dissipate on earth,
the Wintersheimer had effectively entered

00:09:47.170 --> 00:09:48.920
an alternate dimension.

00:09:48.920 --> 00:09:53.380
The airlock opened, and the new recruits were
instructed to step outside and take a look

00:09:53.380 --> 00:09:54.380
around.

00:09:54.380 --> 00:09:59.019
The Wintersheimer veterans informed the new
sailors that everyone on land was likely already

00:09:59.019 --> 00:10:00.769
dead by this point.

00:10:00.769 --> 00:10:05.800
When Sal first exited the submarine, he commented
on everything around him looking eerily similar

00:10:05.800 --> 00:10:08.750
to how it’d looked on land before the mist
descended.

00:10:08.750 --> 00:10:13.380
But with one key difference: It seemed as
though everything was underwater.

00:10:13.380 --> 00:10:18.550
Well, not quite that: It was almost as though
everything was water.

00:10:18.550 --> 00:10:22.269
Like the world had taken on a kind of flowing,
liquid state.

00:10:22.269 --> 00:10:27.400
Sal and the others existed in this otherworldly
land of living water for six months, and as

00:10:27.400 --> 00:10:30.610
the months passed, things only got stranger.

00:10:30.610 --> 00:10:33.959
They found that they neither needed to eat
nor sleep.

00:10:33.959 --> 00:10:38.730
According to Sal, all they did was breathe
- and passed the time by exploring and talking

00:10:38.730 --> 00:10:40.149
to one another.

00:10:40.149 --> 00:10:44.610
Anyone who attempted to take off their suit
would dissolve and diffuse into the same liquid

00:10:44.610 --> 00:10:45.920
that surrounded them.

00:10:45.920 --> 00:10:50.950
Dr. Klutch asked Sal about the other inhabitants
of this alien realm and this was when things

00:10:50.950 --> 00:10:52.800
got truly disturbing.

00:10:52.800 --> 00:10:57.330
There were dead humans and animals floating
all over the place - missing their eyes, as

00:10:57.330 --> 00:11:01.759
though they’d been scooped out, and missing
their mouths, as though they’d been bitten

00:11:01.759 --> 00:11:05.160
out of their face by some kind of huge predator.

00:11:05.160 --> 00:11:09.589
Their empty eye sockets bled constantly, and
Sal theorized that this may have something

00:11:09.589 --> 00:11:14.589
to do with the anomalous blood mists of SCP
- 1861.

00:11:14.589 --> 00:11:18.459
When asked to provide more information on
why all the corpses were mutilated in this

00:11:18.459 --> 00:11:22.940
way, Sal said that one of his superiors on
the Wintersheimer told him “the watcher

00:11:22.940 --> 00:11:26.910
of eyes and biter of teeth deemed them worthy.”

00:11:26.910 --> 00:11:32.889
Whatever this mysterious being was, it seemed
to be a powerful figure within 1861’s water

00:11:32.889 --> 00:11:37.560
world, and Sal felt lucky that he had never
had a direct run-in with the creature himself.

00:11:37.560 --> 00:11:42.959
For his final request, Dr. Klutch asked Sal
to attempt to remove his suit.

00:11:42.959 --> 00:11:48.420
The Foundation had learned in previous instances
of 1861 that the diving suits have anomalous

00:11:48.420 --> 00:11:53.370
durability, and it was impossible for anyone
other than the wearer to remove them - hence

00:11:53.370 --> 00:11:59.180
why the Foundation could never deal with 1861-B
by using brute force.

00:11:59.180 --> 00:12:03.580
Naturally, Klutch was interested in finding
out what was going on underneath.

00:12:03.580 --> 00:12:08.560
Sal expressed fear and anxiety at first, wondering
if after all he’d been through whether he

00:12:08.560 --> 00:12:10.899
could even be considered human anymore.

00:12:10.899 --> 00:12:16.300
Eventually, he was convinced to remove the
suit, and his worst fears were confirmed.

00:12:16.300 --> 00:12:21.509
The second Sal removed his helmet, gallons
of seawater poured out and the now empty suit

00:12:21.509 --> 00:12:22.970
collapsed to the ground.

00:12:22.970 --> 00:12:28.269
Sal’s body was ever found - only some teeth
and a pair of eyes were recovered.

00:12:28.269 --> 00:12:32.850
The eyes were later confirmed as belonging
to a young girl, and the teeth were identified

00:12:32.850 --> 00:12:35.839
as having come from European red deer.

00:12:35.839 --> 00:12:40.500
And so the dark mystery of the HMS Wintersheimer
continues.

00:12:40.500 --> 00:12:44.410
Because of the unpredictable nature of its
appearances, and the resulting difficulty

00:12:44.410 --> 00:12:48.880
of containing it, the Wintersheimer has earned
a Keter Classification.

00:12:48.880 --> 00:12:54.139
The only containment procedure currently employed
by the SCP Foundation is for Mobile Task Forces

00:12:54.139 --> 00:12:59.291
to try and intercept the submarine when appearances
are reported, and hopefully prevent or at

00:12:59.291 --> 00:13:02.949
least reduce the kidnapping of civilians.

00:13:02.949 --> 00:13:05.269
With so many questions left unanswered.

00:13:05.269 --> 00:13:10.370
All we can say for certain is that if a red
mist ever descends on you and a stranger in

00:13:10.370 --> 00:13:15.220
a diving suit tells you that you’re in grave
danger - he’s absolutely right.

00:13:15.220 --> 00:13:21.779
Now go check out “SCP - 035 - The Possessive
Mask” and “SCP - 087 - The Stairwell”

00:13:21.779 --> 00:13:24.170
for more freaky stories from the SCP Foundation!

